                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Here is my \"First Play on Launch Day!\" Video Review:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qiIIRdYaLHM\n\nMy initial instincts looking at this game were right on.  And I should have listened, however I wanted to review it anyhow, and had just enough credit for purchasing it on my account.  And now, well... I will get about my 100th practice run ar refunding a game on Steam.. YAY!  :-P\n\nBugs galore, everything from god awful camera controls and angels, your truck glitching through rocks and terrain, to scoring that makes absolutely no sense.  \n\nThe controls are also a mess, while using WASD makes sense, pretty much every other key doesn't and you cannot map the controls to your own liking either.  \n\nWhile you can upgrade your vehicle with money earned by scoring points while driving to the finish line, that also is buggy and a a slow, tedius process.  It's likely that you'll never want to play enough to actually buy many upgrades anyhow because after spending five to ten minutes in agony trying to work your rig between checkpoints, you'll likely be ready to uninstall and request a refund ASAP!\n\nThe editor you ask?  Half the time when you try to test it by placing your car, the game locks up (for me anyhow), and the editor is a clunky, unresponsive, slow, and unfriendly mess.  It's even more frustrating then playing the levels that come with the game, so no thanks, UGH.\n\nNo, just no.  It scored a 20% in my video review and there's no excuse for this being listed as a final release and not in early access so that at least we could maybe give the developer half of an excuse for a product this bad.",
